# Story 3: Building From Source (40s)
# Hook: Rysh is just Go. Clone it, make build, and run your own binary.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-003-building-from-source.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Rysh is written in Go, so building from source takes just a few commands.

[00:04.0 --> 00:12.0]
Start by cloning the repository and stepping in.

[00:12.0 --> 00:20.0]
Run make build. The Go toolchain compiles a local rysh binary right here.

[00:20.0 --> 00:28.0]
make install copies it into ~/.local/bin so you can run rysh from anywhere.

[00:28.0 --> 00:36.0]
If needed, add ~/.local/bin to your PATH.

[00:36.0 --> 00:40.0]
Confirm with rysh --version and you're building from your own source.

